On Jul 7, 9:57 am, Topi Linkala <n...@iki.fi> wrote:

> As there have been nerfing threads going on I decided to start a new one
> and the topic is: Quest artifact wishing.

Thanks for re-raising this topic. I posted a similar thread a couple
of months ago: search for "YANI: No wishing for quest artifacts
conduct".

> Am I alone thinking that it is very peculiar that everybody but wizard
> can enjoy the Eye without level requirements and everybody but monk can
> do the same to the Eyes.

You're not alone. I proposed splitting off quest artifacts from the
current "artifact-wishless" conduct because unlike, say, Frost Brand,
a role's quest artifact 1) has no chance of being randomly generated
in the dungeon, and 2) in fact requires leaving the dungeon entirely,
via magic portal to the adventurer's homeworld, to retrieve it from
the quest nemesis.

> The only quest artifact that doesn't work properly to others, than those
> who have earned it, is the PYEC.

Actually the Knight's quest artifact is also somewhat restricted, and
there may be one other I'm forgetting. But for the Eye and the Orb,
all neutrals can wish for and use them with abandon.

> If wishing of quest artifacts is allowed shouldn't all of them be nerfed
> to cross-role adventurers? [1]

I would support this, though as I realize these artifacts can be a
major part of one's playing strategy and I don't wish to tell people
how they should play (other than savescumming, which is just
wrong ;-) ), I think my idea of making a separate conduct may keep
more people happy. I think conducts were a great addition to the game
as they allow people to be challenged without making the game harder
for those who just want to win. Of course, I've never wished for a
quest artifact even once and have ascended plenty of times, so I don't
really consider their absence in my particular games a "challenge".

